            <ArticleTitle>Palladium-Catalyzed [5 + 2] Cycloaddition of Vinyloxiranes with Sulfamate-Derived Cyclic Imines To Construct 1,3-Oxazepine Heterocycles.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6268-6271</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02704</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Palladium-catalyzed [5 + 2] cycloaddition of 2-aryl-2-vinyloxiranes with sulfamate-derived cyclic imines is described. The zwitterionic allylpalladium intermediates act as five-membered synthon to react with sulfamate-derived cyclic imines to furnish [5 + 2] cycloaddition, giving 1,3-oxazepine derivatives in moderate to excellent yields with excellent regioselectivities.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
